diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..c1e64cc 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,18 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Deliveries
+
+An event is delivered to a webhook exactly once: when something happens on a board, one `POST` request is sent to the webhook URL for each active webhook subscribed to that action. Deliveries are never retried.
+
+Each request carries these headers:
+
+| Header | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the event happened. |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | `HMAC` using `SHA256` of the request body, signed with the webhook's `signing_secret`. |
+
+The delivery log keeps a week of history. A webhook that fails ten deliveries in a row is deactivated, and an account admin has to reactivate it.
